          {
            "text": "La consulta SQL para BigQuery ha sido validada y es la siguiente:\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n    co.condition_concept_id,\n    cc.concept_name AS condition_concept_name,\n    co.condition_type_concept_id,\n    ctc.concept_name AS condition_type_concept_name,\n    COUNT(co.condition_occurrence_id) AS number_of_episodes,\n    AVG(CAST(DATE_DIFF(co.condition_end_date, co.condition_start_date, DAY) AS BIGNUMERIC)) AS average_duration_days,\n    MIN(DATE_DIFF(co.condition_end_date, co.condition_start_date, DAY)) AS min_duration_days,\n    MAX(DATE_DIFF(co.condition_end_date, co.condition_start_date, DAY)) AS max_duration_days,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(DATE_DIFF(co.condition_end_date, co.condition_start_date, DAY) AS BIGNUMERIC), 4)[OFFSET(1)] AS percentile_25_duration_days,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(DATE_DIFF(co.condition_end_date, co.condition_start_date, DAY) AS BIGNUMERIC), 4)[OFFSET(2)] AS percentile_50_duration_days,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(DATE_DIFF(co.condition_end_date, co.condition_start_date, DAY) AS BIGNUMERIC), 4)[OFFSET(3)] AS percentile_75_duration_days\nFROM\n    `condition_occurrence` AS co\nJOIN\n    `concept` AS cc\n    ON co.condition_concept_id = cc.concept_id\nJOIN\n    `concept` AS ctc\n    ON co.condition_type_concept_id = ctc.concept_id\nWHERE\n    co.condition_end_date IS NOT NULL AND co.condition_start_date IS NOT NULL\nGROUP BY\n    co.condition_concept_id,\n    cc.concept_name,\n    co.condition_type_concept_id,\n    ctc.concept_name\nORDER BY\n    number_of_episodes DESC;\n```\n\n**Explicación de la consulta:**\n\n*   Calcula la duración de cada episodio de condición en días (`DATE_DIFF`).\n*   Filtra los episodios donde `condition_end_date` no es nula para asegurar una duración válida.\n*   Agrupa los resultados por `condition_concept_id` (concepto de la condición) y `condition_type_concept_id` (tipo de la condición), obteniendo los nombres de estos conceptos de la tabla `concept`.\n*   Para cada grupo, calcula:\n    *   El número total de episodios (`number_of_episodes`).\n    *   La duración promedio (`average_duration_days`).\n    *   La duración mínima (`min_duration_days`).\n    *   La duración máxima (`max_duration_days`).\n    *   Los percentiles 25, 50 (mediana) y 75 de la duración (`percentile_25_duration_days`, `percentile_50_duration_days`, `percentile_75_duration_days`) utilizando la función `APPROX_QUANTILES` de BigQuery.\n*   Ordena los resultados de manera descendente por el número de episodios.\n\nEsta consulta te proporcionará una visión detallada de la distribución de la duración de las condiciones, segmentada por sus características clave en el modelo OMOP."
